          "map": "map_world",
          "ratio": "3:2",
          "text": "A container leaves Asia for Europe. There are two ways to get there by sea. The long way: all around Africa, past the Cape of Good Hope. For centuries, it was the only one. The shortcut: through Egypt. It saves about 7,000 km and more than a week at sea. The canal is 193 km of water dug through the desert, between the Mediterranean and the Red Sea. It has no locks: both seas are at the same level.",
