        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "text": "The Suez Canal is the shortest sea route between Asia and Europe. It saves about 7,000 km.\nAbout 12% of world trade depends on it, which makes it a target and a prize: 1956, 1967, 2023.\nOne ship, one storm or one conflict is enough to send global trade the long way around."
